B.a8d=new A.aN("For: clinicians and trainees reasoning through a witnessed paroxysmal event. Not for patients or families to self-assess.\n\nIt does: weigh the features you enter, show which findings pushed the result each way, and suggest a lobe of onset when a focal mechanism is likely.\n\nIt does not: read EEG or imaging, replace video-EEG, decide treatment, or give a validated probability.\n\nYour data: nothing you enter is stored or sent anywhere; it stays in this page and is gone when you close it.",null,B.nr,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.Mu=new A.ej(B.a8d,B.L,null,null,!1,null)
B.Pp=s(["New engine: naive-Bayes log-likelihood model with setting priors and damping of correlated signs.","Weights re-derived from published data with an evidence grade and source for each.","Corrected: ictal crying now favours PNES; urinary incontinence and a normal EEG no longer move the estimate; prolactin also rises after syncope; psychiatric history weighted down.","Added: eyes closed, waxing\u2013waning course, ictal recall, stertorous breathing, presyncopal prodrome, situational triggers, pallor, onset from sleep.","Calgary Syncope\u2013Seizure Score, cardiac and neurological red flags.","Lateralizing signs with side, and a hemisphere estimate.","Video-EEG and ECG results; EEG split into epileptiform vs non-specific.","Weight-of-evidence chart, named patterns, worked examples, copyable summary.","The Tract palette and typography, faster load, shareable URLs for every screen."],t.s)
